  <page_number>189</page_number>
  <running_head>Carolum Rupifortem.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>rare</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">lunt regimen Ecclefiafticum circa illa</l>
    <l n="2">externa distinctum esse à civili seu</l>
    <l n="3">politico.</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">Atque hactenus, vir Clarissime,</l>
    <l n="5">conficitur quam inficeta sit potestas</l>
    <l n="6">Ecclefiastica, quæ instar cinguli ex co-</l>
    <l n="7">rio ductili, elongatur &amp; coarctatur,</l>
    <l n="8">assumitur &amp; deponitur, pro sua cuiquc</l>
    <l n="9">utilitate &amp; prout conducit : quæque</l>
    <l n="10">ad rationes humanas, non Divinas</l>
    <l n="11">accomodatur, &amp; cui nulla accedit au-</l>
    <l n="12">thoritas, præterquam ab injusta occu-</l>
    <l n="13">patione juris alieni, per mendacia, frau-</l>
    <l n="14">des &amp; imposturas, non quidem viro-</l>
    <l n="15">rum sanctorum, qui eam arripuerunt</l>
    <l n="16">cæco judicio, &amp; quia sic mos est; sed</l>
    <l n="17">quorumdam malè animatorum qui</l>
    <l n="18">cæteros in fraudem illiciunt, specie</l>
    <l n="19">pacis, pietatis &amp; juris Divini. Cæte-</l>
    <l n="20">rum pietate &amp; reverentiâ viri impe-</l>
    <l n="21">dior, quominus veteranum illum bel-</l>
    <l n="22">lorum Domini Militem Gisbertum,</l>
    <l n="23">Voetium eruditione &amp; ætate veneran-</l>
    <l n="24">dum, qui in me nuper acrius invectus</l>
    <l n="25">est, ascribam numero illorum, qui po-</l>
    <l n="26">testate suâ Ecclefiastica fucum faciunt,</l>
    <l n="27">sed eorum, qui præjudiciis excæcati</l>
    <l n="28">nequeunt se expedire laqueis, nec libe-</l>
    <l n="29">rare</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Marginal specks and stains only; no legible marginal notes. Running head "Carolum Rupifortem." with page number 189. The last line "rare" is the catchword at the foot right.</notes>
</page>
